\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Cartel repeated-game node under the grim-trigger strategy. Each round a colluding member chooses between maintaining the floor $q_{\mathrm  {floor}}$ or undercutting it by $\varepsilon $. Detection probability $p_d$ slashes the colluder; one-shot defection takes the $\pi _D$ gain once and forfeits future $\pi _C$ stream. The sustainability inequality on the right reduces to the closed-form threshold $p_d^\star $ used in Figure~\ref {fig:cartel-folk}.}}{30}{figure.caption.51}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:cartel-game-inline}{{7}{30}{Cartel repeated-game node under the grim-trigger strategy. Each round a colluding member chooses between maintaining the floor $q_{\mathrm {floor}}$ or undercutting it by $\varepsilon $. Detection probability $p_d$ slashes the colluder; one-shot defection takes the $\pi _D$ gain once and forfeits future $\pi _C$ stream. The sustainability inequality on the right reduces to the closed-form threshold $p_d^\star $ used in Figure~\ref {fig:cartel-folk}}{figure.caption.51}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces A6 --- Repeated-game cartel folk-theorem. Left: sustainability map over the $(p_d, \delta )$ grid; red cells are configurations where the grim-trigger cartel beats one-shot defection in expected PV (sustainable), white cells are where it does not (collapses). The thick black vertical bars mark the per-row threshold $p_d^\star $. Right: mean cartel lifespan (rounds until first detection) vs.\ $p_d$, one line per discount factor $\delta $. At the realistic $\delta = 0.95$, $p_d^\star \approx 0.10$: protocols must achieve $\ge 10\%$ per-round detection to break repeated-game cartels.}}{30}{figure.caption.52}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:cartel-folk}{{8}{30}{A6 --- Repeated-game cartel folk-theorem. Left: sustainability map over the $(p_d, \delta )$ grid; red cells are configurations where the grim-trigger cartel beats one-shot defection in expected PV (sustainable), white cells are where it does not (collapses). The thick black vertical bars mark the per-row threshold $p_d^\star $. Right: mean cartel lifespan (rounds until first detection) vs.\ $p_d$, one line per discount factor $\delta $. At the realistic $\delta = 0.95$, $p_d^\star \approx 0.10$: protocols must achieve $\ge 10\%$ per-round detection to break repeated-game cartels}{figure.caption.52}{}}
